```cedar
// Close work orders at MAIN only with a granted approval for the same work order,
// given by someone other than the agent.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"close_workorder",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input.site_id == "MAIN" &&
  context has approval &&
  context.approval.status == PGI::ApprovalStatus::"APPR" &&
  context.approval.wonum == context.input.wonum &&
  context.approval.site_id == "MAIN" &&
  context.approval.approver != principal
};

// List work orders only when the request is explicitly scoped to MAIN.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"list_workorders",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input has site_id &&
  context.input.site_id has typeChoice0 &&
  context.input.site_id.typeChoice0 == "MAIN" &&
  !(context.input.site_id has typeChoice1)
};
```

The `close_workorder` tool description says not to use it for MAIN. I followed your instruction and allowed closing at MAIN, under the approval conditions above.

I treated "granted" as status `APPR`; `WAPPR` (waiting) and every other status do not count. The approval must also be for MAIN, in addition to matching the work order number. No policy permits `approve_workorder` or any other action, so those stay denied by default.
